All angles are right angles. What is the area of this figure, in $\text{km}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2.5);
\draw (2.1,0.7) rectangle (3.6,1.5);
\node[below,font=\small] at (2,0) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[left,font=\small] at (0,1.25) {$2.5\text{ m}$};
\node[font=\small,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (2.85,0.7) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\node[font=\small,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (3.6,1.1) {$0.8\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A rectangular sign has a rectangular hole cut through it. What is the area of the sign that remains, in $\text{m}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.36]
\draw (0,0) -- (12,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$12\text{ mm}$};
\draw (12,0) -- (12,5) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$5\text{ mm}$};
\draw (12,5) -- (6,9);
\draw (6,9) -- (0,5);
\draw (0,5) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,5) -- (12,5);
\draw[dashed] (6,5) -- (6,9) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$4\text{ mm}$};
\draw (6,5.6) -- (6.6,5.6) -- (6.6,5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The figure is a rectangle with a triangle on top. What is its area, in $\text{mm}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.3]
\draw (0,0) -- (15,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\draw (15,0) -- (15,6);
\draw (15,6) -- (10,10);
\draw (10,10) -- (0,10);
\draw (0,10) -- (0,0) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$10\text{ cm}$};
