All angles are right angles. What is the area of this staircase, in $\text{cm}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.62]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,3);
\draw (3,1.5) rectangle (7,3.5);
\node[below,font=\small] at (2.5,0) {$5\text{ m}$};
\node[left,font=\small] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above,font=\small] at (5,3.5) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (7,2.5) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[font=\small,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,1.5) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[font=\small,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (3,2.25) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Two rectangular tarpaulins are laid on the ground and overlap as shown. What total ground area do they cover, in $\text{m}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75]
\draw (1.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.5,0) -- (3.5,1.5) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.5,1.5) -- (5,1.5);
\draw (5,1.5) -- (5,3.5);
\draw (5,3.5) -- (3.5,3.5);
\draw (3.5,3.5) -- (3.5,5);
\draw (3.5,5) -- (1.5,5);
\draw (1.5,5) -- (1.5,3.5);
\draw (1.5,3.5) -- (0,3.5);
\draw (0,3.5) -- (0,1.5);
\draw (0,1.5) -- (1.5,1.5);
\draw (1.5,1.5) -- (1.5,0);
\draw[gray,thin] (0,1.5) -- (0,-1.2);
\draw[gray,thin] (5,1.5) -- (5,-1.2);
\draw[<->] (0,-1) -- (5,-1) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles are right angles and the four corner pieces removed are identical squares of side $1.5\text{ m}$. What is the area of this figure, in $\text{m}^2$?
